But your sources

53:51.980 --> 53:53.120
seem to offer a different,

53:53.420 --> 53:55.360
maybe more grounded take

53:55.360 --> 53:56.540
on what they're actually doing.

53:56.880 --> 53:58.160
That's a really crucial distinction

53:58.160 --> 53:59.040
and one that gets lost

53:59.040 --> 53:59.740
in a lot of the hype.

54:00.220 --> 54:01.180
LLMs are incredibly

54:01.180 --> 54:01.960
powerful tools,

54:02.060 --> 54:02.400
no doubt.

54:02.400 --> 54:04.420
But what they primarily excel at

54:04.420 --> 54:05.080
