54:23.420 --> 54:24.740
the floor of competence.

54:25.220 --> 54:25.940
Basic writing,

54:26.140 --> 54:26.420
coding,

54:26.740 --> 54:27.200
summarizing,

54:27.320 --> 54:27.900
much easier

54:27.900 --> 54:28.800
for many people now.

54:28.920 --> 54:29.820
But not necessarily

54:29.820 --> 54:30.440
the ceiling.

54:30.440 --> 54:31.660
But they don't necessarily

54:31.660 --> 54:32.680
raise the ceiling

54:32.680 --> 54:34.040
of genuine expertise,

54:34.460 --> 54:34.960
creativity,

54:35.220 --> 54:37.240
or truly groundbreaking insight.

54:37.660 --> 54:38.780
That often involves

54:38.780 --> 54:39.700
challenging assumptions,

54:40.100 --> 54:41.140
synthesizing information

54:41.140 --> 54:42.040
in novel ways,

54:42.460 --> 54:43.700
critical reasoning things

54:43.700 --> 54:44.440
that go beyond

54:44.440 --> 54:45.380
statistical likelihood.

54:45.940 --> 54:47.480
From an RSVP standpoint,

54:47.720 --> 54:49.000
you could characterize LLMs

54:49.000 --> 54:50.500
as incredibly effective

54:50.500 --> 54:52.060
entropy smoothing machines.

54:52.400 --> 54:53.920
They generate highly probable,

54:54.360 --> 54:55.100
low surprise,

54:55.340 --> 54:56.200
average responses

54:56.200 --> 54:57.620
based on their training data,

54:57.620 --> 54:58.960
rather than producing

54:58.960 --> 54:59.820
truly novel,

54:59.980 --> 55:00.700
high information,

55:01.020 --> 55:02.140
or expert-level insights

55:02.140 --> 55:02.960
that might lie

55:02.960 --> 55:03.760
in the long tail

55:03.760 --> 55:05.060
of the probability distribution.

55:05.640 --> 55:06.640
They tend to reduce

55:06.640 --> 55:07.300
the unexpected,

55:07.800 --> 55:08.880
smooth out the anomalies.

55:08.960 --> 55:09.680
Which connects to that

55:09.680 --> 55:11.640
whole weird phantom protocol thing

55:11.640 --> 55:12.620
that was buzzing around

55:12.620 --> 55:13.420
online for a while.

55:13.500 --> 55:14.160
People thought they could

55:14.160 --> 55:15.480
trick LLMs into revealing

55:15.480 --> 55:16.420
hidden personalities

55:16.420 --> 55:17.300
or bypassing

55:17.300 --> 55:18.140
their safety training.

55:18.500 --> 55:18.920
Exactly.

55:19.300 --> 55:20.020
Those episodes

55:20.020 --> 55:21.140
are perfect examples

55:21.140 --> 55:21.980
of what your sources

55:21.980 --> 55:23.660
call placebo role play.

55:24.360 --> 55:25.040
They stem from

55:25.040 --> 55:26.160
a fundamental misunderstanding

55:26.160 --> 55:27.120
of how these models

55:27.120 --> 55:27.860
actually work.

55:28.380 --> 55:29.740
LLMs have context windows,

55:30.340 --> 55:31.680
enormous statistical models,

55:32.060 --> 55:33.120
but they don't have

55:33.120 --> 55:34.080
persistent memory

55:34.080 --> 55:34.820
in the human sense.

55:34.900 --> 55:35.760
They don't have consciousness,

55:36.460 --> 55:36.760
beliefs,

55:36.920 --> 55:38.380
or secret hidden personas

55:38.380 --> 55:39.400
waiting to be unlocked.

55:39.660 --> 55:41.020
So typing phantom

55:41.020 --> 55:41.800
wasn't like

55:41.800 --> 55:43.140
finding a secret T?

55:43.800 --> 55:44.420
Not at all.

55:45.080 --> 55:45.880
Adding a specific

55:45.880 --> 55:46.920
string-like phantom

55:46.920 --> 55:47.680
to a prompt

55:47.680 --> 55:48.640
simply changes

55:48.640 --> 55:49.640
the input context,

55:49.860 --> 55:50.940
which suddenly shifts

55:50.940 --> 55:51.680
the probabilities

55:51.680 --> 55:52.760
of the next tokens

55:52.760 --> 55:53.680
the model generates.

55:54.240 --> 55:55.460
It's functionally isomorphic,

55:55.460 --> 55:56.720
essentially the same mechanism

55:56.720 --> 55:58.640
as simple role play conditioning.

55:58.880 --> 55:59.520
Act like a pirate.

55:59.680 --> 56:00.460
Respond to Shakespeare.

56:01.060 --> 56:02.000
It's not accessing

56:02.000 --> 56:02.960
some hidden depth.

56:03.160 --> 56:04.140
It's just manipulating

56:04.140 --> 56:05.600
the statistics of the output

56:05.600 --> 56:06.840
based on the input prompt.

56:07.520 --> 56:08.500
The idea that needing

56:08.500 --> 56:09.360
billions of outputs

56:09.360 --> 56:10.540
to get something truly novel

56:10.540 --> 56:11.080
is the limit

56:11.080 --> 56:12.660
of the AI's imagination

56:12.660 --> 56:14.340
often reflects an interface

56:14.340 --> 56:15.560
or prompting bottleneck,

56:15.740 --> 56:16.780
not an inherent limit

56:16.780 --> 56:17.540
of the underlying

56:17.540 --> 56:18.400
generative model's

56:18.400 --> 56:19.220
statistical space.

56:19.860 --> 56:20.920
Understanding the underlying

56:20.920 --> 56:21.840
probabilistic,

56:22.280 --> 56:23.020
Markovian nature

56:23.020 --> 56:23.760
helps cut through

56:23.760 --> 56:24.560
the mystification.

56:24.980 --> 56:26.200
Okay, but RSVP

56:26.200 --> 56:27.160
also suggests something

56:27.160 --> 56:27.880
more profound

56:27.880 --> 56:29.060
about AI representations.

56:29.540 --> 56:30.100
Something about

56:30.100 --> 56:31.360
a universal structure.

56:31.540 --> 56:31.960
You mentioned

56:31.960 --> 56:32.740
VEC to VEC.

56:32.900 --> 56:33.960
Yes, this is potentially

56:33.960 --> 56:34.560
revolutionary.

56:34.720 --> 56:34.820
Yeah.

56:35.760 --> 56:37.460
RSVP fundamentally posits

56:37.460 --> 56:38.680
that all representations,

56:39.060 --> 56:39.980
whether in a human brain,

56:40.220 --> 56:41.460
a specific AI model,

56:41.620 --> 56:43.020
