56:47.540 --> 56:49.020
universal scalar vector

56:49.020 --> 56:49.860
entropy field.

56:50.340 --> 56:51.140
Building on this,

56:51.140 --> 56:52.660
your sources detail work

56:52.660 --> 56:53.460
on VEC to VEC,

56:53.840 --> 56:54.720
a method that allows

56:54.720 --> 56:55.420
for the translation

56:55.420 --> 56:56.640
of semantic embeddings,

56:57.120 --> 56:58.360
the internal numerical

56:58.360 --> 56:59.740
representations of meaning

56:59.740 --> 57:00.760
between entirely

57:00.760 --> 57:01.860
different AI models.

57:02.200 --> 57:02.540
Critically,

57:02.620 --> 57:03.100
it can do this

57:03.100 --> 57:03.620
without needing

57:03.620 --> 57:04.860
parallel training data

57:04.860 --> 57:05.920
or shared encoders

57:05.920 --> 57:07.220
or manually defined

57:07.220 --> 57:07.900
anchor points

57:07.900 --> 57:08.640
between the models.

57:08.740 --> 57:09.660
Hey, you can translate

57:09.660 --> 57:11.020
the thoughts of one AI

57:11.020 --> 57:11.720
into the language

57:11.720 --> 57:12.620
of another completely

57:12.620 --> 57:13.320
different AI

57:13.320 --> 57:14.340
without a dictionary.

57:14.660 --> 57:14.960
How?

57:15.240 --> 57:16.420
It works by exploiting

57:16.420 --> 57:17.620
geometric invariances,

57:18.120 --> 57:19.100
assuming both models

57:19.100 --> 57:19.980
are mapping concepts

57:19.980 --> 57:21.500
onto a shared underlying

57:21.500 --> 57:23.420
high-dimensional semantic space.

57:24.440 --> 57:25.480
The astonishing success

57:25.480 --> 57:27.100
of VEC to VEC strongly implies

57:27.100 --> 57:27.740
the existence

57:27.740 --> 57:28.820
of this universal

57:28.820 --> 57:30.540
latent semantic space,

57:30.640 --> 57:31.520
a kind of abstract

57:31.520 --> 57:32.460
platonic structure

57:32.460 --> 57:32.940
of meaning

57:32.940 --> 57:33.840
that all these

57:33.840 --> 57:35.160
diverse AI embeddings

57:35.160 --> 57:36.740
are just different projections

57:36.740 --> 57:37.640
or approximations of.

57:37.800 --> 57:39.220
That means any model's

57:39.220 --> 57:40.100
internal understanding,

57:40.260 --> 57:40.800
its embeddings,

57:40.900 --> 57:41.720
could potentially be

57:41.720 --> 57:43.040
converted, merged,

57:43.140 --> 57:43.480
version,

57:43.660 --> 57:44.780
maybe even searched across,

57:44.860 --> 57:46.000
like using Git for code,

57:46.060 --> 57:47.040
but operating in this

57:47.040 --> 57:48.520
universal category of meaning.

57:48.520 --> 57:50.000
That sounds enormous

57:50.000 --> 57:51.400
for AI interoperability,

57:51.540 --> 57:52.720
maybe even for understanding

57:52.720 --> 57:53.700
meaning itself.

57:54.100 --> 57:54.560
Precisely.

57:54.860 --> 57:55.640
That's the implication.

57:56.240 --> 57:57.160
It allows for true

57:57.160 --> 57:58.040
interoperability,

57:58.200 --> 57:58.940
merging knowledge,

57:59.300 --> 58:00.440
comparing representations

58:00.440 --> 58:01.660
across models built

58:01.660 --> 58:02.560
with totally different

58:02.560 --> 58:03.460
architectures or data.

58:03.740 --> 58:04.820
It breaks down the silos.

58:05.260 --> 58:05.940
It also suggests

58:05.940 --> 58:06.600
that the underlying

58:06.600 --> 58:07.660
RSVP plenum

58:07.660 --> 58:09.380
enforces certain fundamental

58:09.380 --> 58:11.020
entropy-respecting invariants,

58:11.320 --> 58:12.560
things like cycle consistency.

58:12.980 --> 58:13.540
If you translate

58:13.540 --> 58:14.420
from model A to B,

58:14.500 --> 58:15.520
then B back to A,

58:15.820 --> 58:16.400
you should get close

58:16.400 --> 58:17.520
